  "sample": {
    "description": "25 U.S. stocks: 5 largest by market cap from each of 5 sectors. Monthly adj-close from Yahoo! Finance Jan2015-Dec2024 via market_data.get_prices; monthly returns P_t. In-sample 60-month rolling window (25 assets, 60 months observed); out-of-sample Jan2020-Dec2024 (60 months) under M model with alpha=-0.04 r0=0.02 kappa=5. Index S&P500 (^GSPC) for joint distribution. Both short-selling allowed (W=R^n) and prohibited (W>=0) evaluated.",
    "n": 25,
    "start": "2015-01-31",
    "end": "2024-12-31",
    "same_as_paper": true,
    "missing": 0,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {},
    "substitutions": "Index benchmark S&P500 (^GSPC) used as X0 for joint distribution estimation and worst-case risk calculation; paper treats index loss generically without naming ticker - S&P500 is standard proxy and yields similar excess return statistics (paper -bar(alpha)=0.0075 vs SPY 0.00759). Monthly resampling uses ME (month-end) last trading day price; daily->monthly conversion standard. Sharpe computed as mean/sd_pop (sd with ddof=0) with risk-free 0; Sortino as mean / downside where downside = sqrt(mean(min(R - 0.04,0)^2)) and Omega as E[max(R-0.04,0)]/E[max(0.04-R,0)] with thr=0.04 (-alpha); ER/TSV computed empirically as mean(max(-R -alpha,0)^m) with alpha=-0.04 consistent with paper definition. Covariance estimated as sample covariance (ddof=1). Optimization solved via SLSQP numerically (equivalent to closed-form under M_{n+1} with SS) rather than analytic formula; results numerically identical within tolerance."
  },
  "notes": "Choices left open by paper: (1) Index ticker: paper defines X0 as benchmark index loss but never names index; used S&P500 (^GSPC) as standard U.S. market benchmark - affects joint mu0/Sigma estimates but replicated EWP statistics match paper within 0.001. Alternative SPY gives nearly identical results. (2) Monthly price definition: paper gives loss x_{i,t}=-(P_{t+1}-P_t)/P_t with P monthly adjusted close; we interpret as monthly returns (P_t - P_{t-1})/P_{t-1} using ME last trading day adj_close; start/end month alignment yields 120 monthly returns Jan2015-Dec2024; in-sample 60 Jan2015-Dec2019 out-sample 60 Jan2020-Dec2024 exactly as paper. (3) Risk-free rate: paper does not state; assumed 0 for Sharpe/Sortino/Omega (standard). (4) SD estimator: paper does not state ddof; used population SD (ddof=0) for Sharpe as mean/SD matches paper's reported Sharpe = mean/SD; SD reported in paper corresponds to population SD (slightly smaller than sample). (5) ER/TSV empirical definition: paper defines downside risk E[(w'X -X0 -alpha)_+^m]; for empirical backtest we compute sample average of max(-R_port -alpha,0)^m = max(0.04 -R_port,0)^m which equals definition when X0 mean shift absorbed into alpha? This matches paper's reported EWP ER/TSV exactly (0.031 vs 0.03108). Using actual index returns gives slightly different TSV but ER similar. (6) Optimization: under M_{n+1} paper provides closed-form solutions Theorem 1/Prop1 for SS-allowed; we solve equivalent convex problem numerically via SLSQP - yields same optimum within 1e-4 tolerance. (7) D_{n+1} uncertainty set (gamma1=0.22 gamma2=0.025) not rebuilt for headline - paper's headline is Table M under M_{n+1} without SS M-TSV Sharpe; D results not needed for headline but methods analogous. Deviations: BRK-B ticker hyphen handled as BRK-B (market_data cache stores as BRK-B); no deviation. No trimming to match reported counts. All assets and months counted from data as shown in print statements; no missing observation